---
title: "Does the gh budget hold, and does the call log keep each full log?"
config:
  markdownAutoWrap: false
  state:
    useMaxWidth: false
---
stateDiagram-v2
  classDef plain fill:#f4f6f7,stroke:#566573,color:#1b2631
  classDef plainWrong fill:#f4f6f7,stroke:#c0392b,stroke-width:4px,color:#7b241c
  classDef group0 fill:#d1f2eb,stroke:#697976,color:#1b2631
  classDef group1 fill:#d6eaf8,stroke:#6b757c,color:#1b2631
  classDef group2 fill:#fdebd0,stroke:#7f7668,color:#1b2631
  classDef group2Wrong fill:#fdebd0,stroke:#c0392b,stroke-width:4px,color:#7b241c
  classDef group3 fill:#f9d6d5,stroke:#7d6b6b,color:#1b2631
  classDef group3Wrong fill:#f9d6d5,stroke:#c0392b,stroke-width:4px,color:#7b241c
  state "Legend" as legend {
    state "Budget kept, above the floor" as legendGroup0
    state "Budget kept, at the floor" as legendGroup1
    state "A call under the floor" as legendGroup2
    state "A whole log lost" as legendGroup3
    state "Breaks a rule today" as legendWrong
  }
  class legendGroup0 group0
  class legendGroup1 group1
  class legendGroup2 group2
  class legendGroup3 group3
  class legendWrong plainWrong
  state "At the same time" as regions {
    [*] --> r0s0
    state "The API budget above the<br/>floor" as r0s0
    state "The API budget at the<br/>floor" as r0s1
    state "The API budget spent" as r0s2
    r0s0 --> r0s1 : the API answers the call and<br/>counts it [when a call under<br/>way, the call log has room, no<br/>old log or a call under way,<br/>the call log past its size, no<br/>old log]
    %% when r1s6, r1s8
    r0s1 --> r0s2 : the API answers the call and<br/>counts it [unless a call under<br/>way, the call log has room, no<br/>old log or a pass held, the<br/>call log has room, the old log<br/>keeps the last full log or a<br/>pass held, the call log past<br/>its size, no old log or no<br/>call, the call log has room,<br/>the old log keeps the last<br/>full log or no call, the call<br/>log past its size, no old log]
    %% when not r1s6, r1s12, r1s13, r1s18, r1s19
    --
    [*] --> r1s15
    state "a call starts at the<br/>floor, no call log, the<br/>old log keeps the last<br/>full log" as r1s0
    state "a call starts at the<br/>floor, the call log has<br/>room, the old log keeps<br/>the last full log" as r1s1
    state "a call starts at the<br/>floor, the call log past<br/>its size, no old log" as r1s2
    state "a call under way, no call<br/>log, a full log lost" as r1s3
    state "a call under way, no call<br/>log, no old log" as r1s4
    state "a call under way, no call<br/>log, the old log keeps the<br/>last full log" as r1s5
    state "a call under way, the call<br/>log has room, no old log" as r1s6
    state "a call under way, the call<br/>log has room, the old log<br/>keeps the last full log" as r1s7
    state "a call under way, the call<br/>log past its size, no old<br/>log" as r1s8
    state "a pass held, no call log,<br/>no old log" as r1s9
    state "a pass held, the call log<br/>has room, a full log lost" as r1s10
    state "a pass held, the call log<br/>has room, no old log" as r1s11
    state "a pass held, the call log<br/>has room, the old log<br/>keeps the last full log" as r1s12
    state "a pass held, the call log<br/>past its size, no old log" as r1s13
    state "a pass held, the call log<br/>past its size, the old log<br/>keeps the last full log" as r1s14
    state "no call, no call log, no<br/>old log" as r1s15
    state "no call, the call log has<br/>room, a full log lost" as r1s16
    state "no call, the call log has<br/>room, no old log" as r1s17
    state "no call, the call log has<br/>room, the old log keeps<br/>the last full log" as r1s18
    state "no call, the call log past<br/>its size, no old log" as r1s19
    state "no call, the call log past<br/>its size, the old log<br/>keeps the last full log" as r1s20
    r1s0 --> r1s5 : the API answers the call and<br/>counts it
    r1s0 --> r1s1 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s1 --> r1s7 : the API answers the call and<br/>counts it
    r1s2 --> r1s8 : the API answers the call and<br/>counts it
    r1s2 --> r1s0 : the process renames the log to<br/>the old log
    r1s3 --> r1s16 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s3 --> r1s10 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s4 --> r1s17 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s4 --> r1s6 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s4 --> r1s11 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s5 --> r1s18 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s5 --> r1s7 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s5 --> r1s12 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s6 --> r1s19 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log [when The API budget above<br/>the floor]
    %% when r0s0
    r1s6 --> r1s8 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log
    r1s6 --> r1s13 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log [when The API budget above<br/>the floor]
    %% when r0s0
    r1s7 --> r1s20 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log [when The API budget<br/>spent]
    %% when r0s2
    r1s7 --> r1s14 : the call's line goes in the<br/>log [when The API budget<br/>spent]
    %% when r0s2
    r1s7 --> r1s3 : the process renames the log to<br/>the old log [when The API<br/>budget spent]
    %% when r0s2
    r1s8 --> r1s2 : a pass starts a gh call in a<br/>free slot [when The API budget<br/>at the floor]
    %% when r0s1
    r1s8 --> r1s5 : the process renames the log to<br/>the old log [unless The API<br/>budget above the floor]
    %% when not r0s0
    r1s9 --> r1s15 : a pass reads the budget above<br/>the floor and goes on
    r1s9 --> r1s15 : another pass's answer is<br/>there, and the pass takes it
    r1s9 --> r1s15 : the pass asks the API what is<br/>left and keeps the answer
    r1s15 --> r1s4 : a pass starts a gh call in a<br/>free slot
    r1s15 --> r1s9 : the pass reads the budget at<br/>the floor, or the API gives no<br/>answer, and it holds
    r1s18 --> r1s12 : a pass reads the budget at the<br/>floor and holds
  }
  class r0s0 group0
  class r0s1 plain
  class r0s2 plain
  class r1s0 group2Wrong
  class r1s1 group2Wrong
  class r1s2 group2Wrong
  class r1s3 group3Wrong
  class r1s4 group0
  class r1s5 group1
